## How the troop runs advancement

These apply to any advancement planning — rank or merit badge, Target First
Class or Target Eagle:

- **Abbreviations** — note any troop-specific shorthand (e.g. "SMC" for
  Scoutmaster Conference and "BoR" for Board of Review).
- **Scoutmaster conferences and boards of review** — describe whether/how they
  appear on the calendar (e.g. inside regular meetings vs. scheduled
  separately).
- **Per-meeting capacity** — describe the real constraint on how many
  conferences or boards can be scheduled per meeting, and whether they can run
  concurrently.
- **Who can sign off what** — describe which adult roles can sign off merit
  badge requirements, run boards of review, and run Scoutmaster conferences.
- **Any standard shorthand for the closing rank requirements** (Scout Spirit,
  Scoutmaster conference, board of review).
- **Any recurring troop-specific events** relevant to advancement planning
  (e.g. an intensive sign-off day) — describe format, duration, adult
  leader turnout, and how much of the conference/board load it typically
  absorbs.
